{"status":"success","data":[{"siteid":13478,"sitename":"Over Gunnarsfjorden","sitedescription":"Glacial origin lake. Metamorphic rocks, mostly micaceous and garnetiferous schists and slates of Caledonian. age (ca 550–400Ma), predominate the catchment. Local vegetation is tundra, dwarf shrub communities dominated by Empetrum nigrum ssp. hermaphroditum, with Vaccinium spp. and Betula nana.","geography":"{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[[[28.16545,71.03753],[28.17268,71.03753],[28.17268,71.03858],[28.16545,71.03858],[28.16545,71.03753]]]}","altitude":75,"recdatecreated":"2016-08-09T15:51:42.000Z","collectionunits":[{"handle":"GUNNARS","datasets":[{"datasetid":20282,"datasettype":"geochronologic"}],"collectionunit":null,"collectionunitid":15100,"collectionunittype":"Core"}]}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}